<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Error codes — ALN Table Saw</title>
<style>{{ style }}</style>
</head>
<body>
<main>

<header class="code-head sev-info">
  <div class="code-id">Codes</div>
  <h1 class="code-title">Table saw thermal supervisor</h1>
  <p class="code-summary">Every code the supervisor can show, what it means, and what to
  do about it. All of it is stored on the saw — none of these pages need the internet.</p>
</header>

{% for group, items in groups %}
<h2>{{ group }}</h2>
<ul class="code-list">
{% for d in items %}
  <li><a class="sev-{{ d.severity }}" href="{{ d.code }}.html">
    <span class="id">{{ d.code }}</span>
    <span class="txt"><strong>{{ d.title }}</strong><span>{{ d.summary }}</span></span>
  </a></li>
{% endfor %}
</ul>
{% endfor %}

<h2>Reading the status LED</h2>
<p>The LED on the supervisor board is the only indicator visible at the machine. It tells
you the family of problem; these pages tell you the rest. Warnings
({% for d in warnings %}{{ d.code }}{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %})
leave the LED <strong>solid</strong> — the saw keeps running and the only place they are
announced is the web dashboard. These pages tell you what to do about them.</p>

<section class="refs">
<h2>The project</h2>
{% for ref in repo_refs %}
<div class="ref">
  {% if ref.qr %}<div class="qr">{{ ref.qr }}</div>{% endif %}
  <div>
    <div class="ref-title">{{ ref.title }}</div>
    <div class="ref-url">{{ ref.url }}</div>
  </div>
</div>
{% endfor %}
</section>

<footer>
<p>Error code registry {{ registry_version }} &middot; built from {{ commit }} ({{ commit_date }})</p>
<p>Codes are append-only: a published code never changes meaning and is never reused.</p>
</footer>

</main>
</body>
</html>
